<title>TANZANIA: TANZANIAN SHILLING GAINS ON DOLLAR, STERLING.</title>
<headline>TANZANIAN SHILLING GAINS ON DOLLAR, STERLING.</headline>
<dateline>DAR ES SALAAM 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tanzanian shilling continued to make strong gains against both the dollar and sterling due to a surplus of foreign exchange in the local market, the central Bank of Tanzania (BoT) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Against the dollar, the shilling traded at a mean rate of 619.8687 against Friday's 620.3934. It traded at 984.6646 against the pound from Friday's 994.7707.</p>
